{
  "version": 2,
  "_comment": "Phase 4 — the real Secret Drawer puzzle. Source of truth: Secret-Drawer-Items (NEW2).docx + Secret-Drawer-Playbook.docx (off-repo, on Thomas's Desktop). Background: real photos of Thomas's actual drawer (meme stickers baked in as permanent flavor). Two view states (`junk-*` wide top-down vs `secret-*` close-up of the recessed compartments) × two dust states (clean / dusty) = four surfaces. The wide junk view is the start; chain 8 (padlock) gates the transition to the secret view. Every puzzle item is an engine overlay placed on top. Chains land in commit-sized batches; each chain commit bumps the theme version. The engine's full action-verb surface is documented in the docblock of drawer-engine.js — Phase 4 adds: `video`, `fullscreen`, `passcode`, and `require` (interaction-level flag preconditions). Coordinates were placed in ?author mode and baked back here as the layout pass for each chain batch.",

  "_chains": {
    "0-todo":       "You Got This notebook → click → to-do clue (Find Ring · Tidy drawer · Dust + scribbled notes)",
    "1-start":      "screwdriver + screw → dust appears → duster clears it → reveals duck pin (Top Prize path). Leaving dust = Golden Egg path.",
    "2-hulk":       "Hulk + hammer → armed Hulk → smash silver nugget → Rings (Find Ring ✓). Torch on Rings → 'one PEZ dispenser to rule them all'. Click PEZ → Auction Receipt ($264M Faberge foreshadow).",
    "3-duck":       "Mini Pump + small duck → midway duck → giant duck. Click giant duck → fullscreen browser crush. Pineapple duck is a one-liner easter egg.",
    "4-scroll":     "BIC Lighter + Rolled Scroll → Bitcoin whitepaper clue. BIC + Jack-o-Lantern → pumpkin lit. The BIC stays in the drawer for both.",
    "5-hotwheels":  "STUB until Thomas + Daniel film the bracket. 13.5 sticker (hover hint) + two race cars + Hot Rod collectible. Click any car → 'race video coming soon' clue.",
    "6-glasses":    "Ensure (alertness) → Glasses Case → Eyeglasses → combine with Clip-Ons → Sunglasses → click reveals the Elf prelude ('See you again Dec. 1st 2026...'). Fugglers Notebook is the in-puzzle hint for the clip-on combine.",
    "7-batteries":  "Car Keys → Toy Train (unlocks battery cover) → AAA Batteries → Train ready → click → chugs. iPhone is direct: click → muted family videos.",
    "9-hangman":    "Combine Sticky Notes + Mechanical Pencil → Hangman mini-game. Word picked from the current month's 20-word rotation (top-level `hangman` block). Win sets flag `hangman-won`. Re-playable."
  },

